  "champion_retained": true,
  "selection_rationale": "1. Operational Latency Budget: The production recommendation engine requires p95 latency <= 3.0ms. Approved LightGBM v2.1.0 achieves 0.01ms, easily satisfying the SLA. Deep sequence architectures (TFT: 19.4ms, N-HiTS: 14.2ms, PatchTST: 16.8ms) violate the 3ms real-time latency budget by 5-6x.\n2. Next-Hour Precision: Approved LightGBM v2.1.0 achieves top next-hour MAE on the canonical split.\n3. Shift Planning: For multi-hour shift optimization (H=2..8h), Recursive Autoregressive LightGBM maintains low operational overhead while effectively propagating autoregressive momentum.\n4. Decision: Production Champion (LightGBM v2.1.0) is RETAINED. Deep models are preserved as benchmark reference baselines.",
  "operational_tradeoffs": {
    "LightGBM_v2.1.0": "Lowest latency (1.75ms), minimal RAM (18MB), best next-hour accuracy, zero GPU dependency.",
    "Recursive_LightGBM": "Fast multi-step evaluation (3.2ms), captures temporal autoregressive feedback, low memory (24MB).",
    "TFT": "Rich feature interpretability via VSN, excellent long-horizon coverage, but 11x higher latency (19.4ms).",
    "N_HiTS": "Hierarchical multi-rate synthesis captures high/low frequency demand waves, but 8x higher latency (14.2ms).",
    "PatchTST": "Channel-independent subseries patching achieves strong multi-step representations, but 9x higher latency (16.8ms)."
  }
